Alembic migrations for WealthPilot.

Run from backend/:

    uv run alembic upgrade head                        # apply
    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "msg"    # create from model changes
    uv run alembic check                               # fail if models and DB disagree
    uv run alembic downgrade -1                        # step back one

Conventions
-----------
* The database URL comes from app.config.Settings (database_url_sync, psycopg),
  set in env.py. There is no URL in alembic.ini, so no password is committed.
* Constraint and index names come from the naming convention in app/db/base.py.
  Never rely on a Postgres-generated name: a later migration has to drop it by
  name.
* env.py ignores tables whose name starts with "checkpoint". Those belong to
  LangGraph's Postgres checkpointer, which creates them through its own setup();
  without the filter, every autogenerate would propose dropping them.
* Generated revisions are passed through `ruff check --fix` and `ruff format`
  by the post_write_hooks in alembic.ini, so they meet the same standard as
  hand-written code.
* Always read an autogenerated revision before applying it. Autogenerate does
  not detect server-side defaults on computed columns, table or column renames
  (it sees a drop plus an add), or anything outside Base.metadata such as
  extensions, roles, grants and views.

Still to come
-------------
The read-only Postgres role and the v_* views that model-generated SQL runs
against (ARCHITECTURE section 5) arrive with the portfolio agent in Phase 4.
They are deliberately migrations rather than a docker init script, so that
local and RDS take the same path.
